  "findings": [
    "No API read exists for on-chain authorisation state or for the outbox status of a queued claimProduct/setIssuer. `GET /passports/:id/anchor` returns a queue, but filtered to `kind: \"anchor\"`, and `GET /passports/:id/claim` covers only the claim. So an operator UI cannot tell a supplier \"your authorisation is still pending\" — it can only retry the upload and read the 403. This script waits on `authorized[productId][issuer]` over JSON-RPC instead, which is what the upload route and any verifier do, but it is a gap in the browser-drivable surface.",
    "The public export bundle carries no anchoring transaction hash, so an independent verifier has to sweep `eth_getLogs` to find the anchor — which on a range-capped free-tier endpoint exhausts its request budget and yields an honest but useless \"inconclusive\". `verify-passport.mjs` already accepts an `anchorTxHash` member (a hint; the log found there is still fully checked against the registry, the topic, the productId, the version and the recomputed root). Emitting it from `GET /api/public/passports/:id/export` would cost one column read and remove the sweep entirely. This script attaches it from the chain so the exported bundle in scripts/out/ is directly verifiable."
  ],
